{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Identifying Known Users","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Identifying-Known-Users"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Appcues recommends choosing opaque and hard to guess user IDs, such as a UUID. See the "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/docs.appcues.com\/article\/159-faq#choosing-a-user-id","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for more details about how to choose a User ID."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Note"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/identify(userID:properties:)","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is recommended that the application identify a user at moments such as sign in, and also when the app starts up on a cold launch with existing log in credentials. This will ensure that any user properties tied to this user can be kept accurately up to date."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The inverse of identifying is resetting. For example, if a user logs out of your app. Calling "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/reset()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" will disable tracking of screens and events until a user is identified again."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you have special security needs and your account has been configured to use the Appcues identity verification feature, follow the steps outlined in the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/docs.appcues.com\/dev-installing-appcues\/identity-verification","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", when calling "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/identify(userID:properties:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Identifying Anonymous Users","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Identifying-Anonymous-Users"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/anonymous()","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The format of anonymous IDs can customized with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/Config\/anonymousIDFactory(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Anonymous IDs will always be prefixed with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anon:"},{"type":"text","text":" by the SDK."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Grouping Users","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Grouping-Users"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Associating a user with a group allows you to additionally capture analytics at the group level, and target content to show based upon group membership and properties."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/group(groupID:properties:)","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To ensure the most accurate content targeting based upon group information, it’s recommended to supply the group information immediately after a new user is identified."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit"],["doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit","doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"In order to target content to the right users at the right time, you need to identify users and send Appcues data about them.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Tracking","doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/URLSchemeC